I'll create a Zephyr template for a three-across product row with your requirements.

```zephyr
{* Fetch products from content feed, requiring images *}
{content = api_content(
    count=3,
    filter="images.thumb.url IS NOT NULL"
)}

{* Abort send if we don't have 3 products with images *}
{if content.size() < 3}
    {abort}
{/if}

{* Three-column product row *}
<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
    <tr>
        {foreach content as product}
        <td width="33%" align="center" valign="top" style="padding: 10px;">
            {* Product Image *}
            <a href="{product.url}" style="display:block;">
                <img src="{product.images.thumb.url}" alt="{product.title}" width="180" style="max-width:100%; height:auto; display:block;" />
            </a>

            {* Product Title *}
            <a href="{product.url}" style="display:block; color:#333; text-decoration:none; font-size:14px; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10px;">
                {product.title}
            </a>

            {* Product Price *}
            <div style="color:#666; font-size:16px; margin-top:5px;">
                ${product.price}
            </div>
        </td>
        {/foreach}
    </tr>
</table>
```

**Key features:**
- **`filter="images.thumb.url IS NOT NULL"`** ensures only products with images are fetched
- **`{if content.size() < 3}{abort}{/if}`** prevents send if fewer than 3 products are available
- **Hero product preservation**: The `api_content()` call respects pinned items in Recommendations automatically—the pinned product will be included in the returned set
- **Table layout**: Uses email-safe HTML table for reliable 3-column rendering across email clients

If you need to adjust the image path (e.g., `product.images.full.url` instead of `thumb`), price formatting (cents, currency symbol), or want responsive stacking on mobile, let me know!
